    {
      "block_id": "p0001-b0013",
      "page_number": 1,
      "reading_order": 13,
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "semantic_role": "lesson_content",
      "source_text": "Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth was flat. However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of the first to suggest that the Earth is spherical. Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how ships disappear over the horizon and how the Earth's shadow on the Moon is curved during a lunar eclipse. Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further confirmed that the Earth is round.",
      "required_for_coverage": true,
      "provenance": {
